WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.110 --> 00:00:05.160
In Westworld Season 2 Episode 6, Maeve stands
surrounded by corpses.

00:00:05.160 --> 00:00:10.070
These are the hosts who charged her last episode
– she’s apparently killed them, with her

00:00:10.070 --> 00:00:12.450
voice power, and her swords.

00:00:12.450 --> 00:00:14.419
Did she really have to do this?

00:00:14.419 --> 00:00:16.530
Her voice can control hosts.

00:00:16.530 --> 00:00:20.740
Why not just “Freeze” them, like Maeve
did to Bernard last season ? Or wake them

00:00:20.740 --> 00:00:26.020
to consciousness, like Maeve offered to Akane
? Maeve told Bernard she won’t hurt him

00:00:26.020 --> 00:00:31.420
because that’s what humans do to hosts . But
here she is, slaughtering dozens of helpless

00:00:31.420 --> 00:00:36.470
hosts, which arguably makes her no better
than the humans she’s rebelling against.

00:00:36.470 --> 00:00:41.640
Akane mourns the death of Sakura, and Maeve
remembers her own beloved daughter – it’s

00:00:41.640 --> 00:00:47.329
a comment on the sameness of human stories
and feelings across cultures, and a reflection

00:00:47.329 --> 00:00:50.400
on the preciousness of host life.

00:00:50.400 --> 00:00:53.540
And then Maeve kills more soldiers, cause
fuck those guys.

00:00:53.540 --> 00:00:57.960
They’re confronted by Tanaka, who’s challenged
to a duel by Musashi.

00:00:57.960 --> 00:01:03.440
Musashi uses two swords in combat, just like
the real historical Miyamoto Musashi who was

00:01:03.440 --> 00:01:05.190
famous for using two swords.

00:01:05.190 --> 00:01:11.390
Akane asks Maeve to use her power on Tanaka,
but Maeve says “We each deserve … to choose

00:01:11.390 --> 00:01:12.630
our fate.

00:01:12.630 --> 00:01:14.540
Even if that fate … is death”.

00:01:14.540 --> 00:01:19.680
So Musashi beats Tanaka, and lets him commit
seppuku before beheading him – allowing

00:01:19.680 --> 00:01:21.460
Tanaka to choose death.

00:01:21.460 --> 00:01:28.590
But does Tanaka or Musashi, or any of the
Shogun hosts really have the power to choose?

00:01:28.590 --> 00:01:32.590
Even if they’re off their scripts, their
personalities are still programmed, they’re

00:01:32.590 --> 00:01:36.210
not fully conscious, and they don’t know
that their world is fake.

00:01:36.210 --> 00:01:42.260
How can they truly choose death when they
don’t know the nature of their lives?

00:01:42.260 --> 00:01:48.220
They go to Snow Lake, and lay Sakura’s heart
to rest in the place she felt at peace . Maeve

00:01:48.220 --> 00:01:52.660
heads off to find her daughter, while Akane
and Musashi stay behind.

00:01:52.660 --> 00:01:57.600
They choose to defend their land and stay
with Sakura’s spirit – even if it means

00:01:57.600 --> 00:02:00.810
their death when Delos or other hosts come.

00:02:00.810 --> 00:02:04.810
Would their choice be different if they knew
that their “land” is a theme park, and

00:02:04.810 --> 00:02:06.840
that Sakura is a broken robot?

00:02:06.840 --> 00:02:12.200
As this inscription says, “everything is
a dream” – this place is fake.

00:02:12.200 --> 00:02:18.810
And maybe there’s beauty in choosing the
illusion – like religious faith, love, meaning.

00:02:18.810 --> 00:02:23.310
But if Delos restores the park, these hosts
could be trapped in the same cycle of death

00:02:23.310 --> 00:02:26.090
and abuse that Maeve fought to escape.

00:02:26.090 --> 00:02:29.760
It seems wrong to leave them in danger and
ignorance.

00:02:29.760 --> 00:02:33.599
But maybe it’d also be wrong for Maeve wake
them against their will.

00:02:33.599 --> 00:02:38.550
It’s similar to the real-world ethics of
visiting uncontacted peoples – maybe they

00:02:38.550 --> 00:02:44.709
have the right to choose to keep traditional
lifestyles . But can you choose when you don’t

00:02:44.709 --> 00:02:46.560
know the outside world?

00:02:46.560 --> 00:02:51.440
Hanaryo joins Maeve’s party as they exit
Shogunworld through a grave tunnel.

00:02:51.440 --> 00:02:55.970
The way this works is that undertaker hosts
‘bury’ dead hosts by chucking them in

00:02:55.970 --> 00:03:01.319
these tunnels, where they’re taken underground
to the Mesa for repairs – so Westworld handles

00:03:01.319 --> 00:03:04.620
dead without breaking the illusion of the
park.

00:03:04.620 --> 00:03:07.599
Maeve finally reunites with her daughter.

00:03:07.599 --> 00:03:13.120
They had lived at this homestead until about
a year ago, when William killed them both.

00:03:13.120 --> 00:03:17.150
Maeve broke down, and was reprogrammed as
the Mariposa madam.

00:03:17.150 --> 00:03:21.440
Now when she returns, she finds her daughter
has a new mother.

00:03:21.440 --> 00:03:25.190
Maeve was replaced, just like Clementine was
when she was decommissioned.

00:03:25.190 --> 00:03:30.260
This is how Westworld works – for all we
know, this daughter had a dozen mothers besides

00:03:30.260 --> 00:03:31.260
Maeve.

00:03:31.260 --> 00:03:32.930
So how can Maeve claim her?

00:03:32.930 --> 00:03:37.940
At the start of the season, Bernarnold said
something’s “real” when it’s “irreplaceable”

00:03:37.940 --> 00:03:39.940
. Maeve’s been replaced.

00:03:39.940 --> 00:03:42.930
So is her relationship with her daughter “real”?

00:03:42.930 --> 00:03:48.080
Just when things get philosophical, Ghost
Nation turns up, and chases Maeve and her

00:03:48.080 --> 00:03:49.080
daughter.

00:03:49.080 --> 00:03:53.940
This has happened before – Maeve remembers
being chased and scalped back in Season 1.

00:03:53.940 --> 00:03:59.390
But this time, Akecheta tells Maeve to come
with him, that they “are meant for the same

00:03:59.390 --> 00:04:04.190
path” . Maeve replies that his “path leads
to hell” . Last season, Maeve learned that

00:04:04.190 --> 00:04:09.190
the Ghost Nation religion involves shades
– figures of Westworld techs.

00:04:09.190 --> 00:04:13.890
Shades are described as men “sent from hell
to oversee our world” . So maybe that’s

00:04:13.890 --> 00:04:16.410
why Maeve associates Ghost Nation with “hell”.

00:04:16.410 --> 00:04:18.459
But isn’t Maeve woke now?

00:04:18.459 --> 00:04:23.199
Doesn’t she know that shades are just techs,
and hell’s just the Mesa, and hosts get

00:04:23.199 --> 00:04:24.199
replaced?

00:04:24.199 --> 00:04:26.629
Isn’t she curious about Ghost Nation?

00:04:26.629 --> 00:04:30.069
And why is she running away instead of using
her voice on the hosts?

00:04:30.069 --> 00:04:35.080
Maeve’s meant to have maxed-out intelligence
. Maybe her daughter and homestead have made

00:04:35.080 --> 00:04:37.889
Maeve fall back to old patterns.

00:04:37.889 --> 00:04:43.289
As a conscious host, she has to balance the
programmed feelings that give her life meaning

00:04:43.289 --> 00:04:48.560
against the complex realities that undermine
meaning – just like real life.

00:04:48.560 --> 00:04:53.419
Lee calls Delos security for help, which could
save Felix, Sylvester and Lee.

00:04:53.419 --> 00:04:57.689
But it’s a betrayal of Maeve, putting her
hosts in danger.

00:04:57.689 --> 00:05:00.500
Lee at least has the decency to look guilty.

00:05:00.500 --> 00:05:05.270
After the time he’s spent with Maeve, he
sees that hosts are people too.

00:05:05.270 --> 00:05:09.520
William spends some quality time with his
daughter Emily, aka Grace.

00:05:09.520 --> 00:05:14.870
At first, Bill thinks she’s a host, sent
by Ford . He tells her to evacuate to safety,

00:05:14.870 --> 00:05:18.180
but she proves her worth by stopping a host
ambush.

00:05:18.180 --> 00:05:20.699
Later, she and Bill have a heart to heart.

00:05:20.699 --> 00:05:24.930
They talk about going to the Raj once with
Juliet, Emily’s mother.

00:05:24.930 --> 00:05:29.969
But Emily and Bill have different memories
of that time . Some fans take this as evidence

00:05:29.969 --> 00:05:33.330
that William is a host, failing a fidelity
test.

00:05:33.330 --> 00:05:37.370
But maybe he’s just a bad dad who forgets
stuff about his kid.

00:05:37.370 --> 00:05:42.099
Emily says she wants to bring Bill home – to
repair their relationship, and to save Bill

00:05:42.099 --> 00:05:47.150
from dying in the park . Bill agrees, but
in the morning, he leaves Emily behind to

00:05:47.150 --> 00:05:48.819
continue his quest.

00:05:48.819 --> 00:05:54.029
So this is classic Bill – he acts like a
“good guy” and a “Family man” . But

00:05:54.029 --> 00:05:59.800
that’s just to hide his true Westworld self
. Emily is also hiding something.

00:05:59.800 --> 00:06:04.949
She says she only came to the parks for nostalgia,
and now wants to leave . But earlier, Emily

00:06:04.949 --> 00:06:10.020
told Stubbs that she’s not looking to leave
, and we saw her following this map with the

00:06:10.020 --> 00:06:11.580
Delos research symbol.

00:06:11.580 --> 00:06:15.759
It looks like Emily has a mission that she’s
hiding from William.

00:06:15.759 --> 00:06:20.460
She mentions being contacted by Charlotte
. So maybe she’s actually working for Charlotte,

00:06:20.460 --> 00:06:26.630
helping her secure Delos data – and if William
is a robot, maybe he’s the data.

00:06:26.630 --> 00:06:29.419
We don’t yet know what Emily really wants.

00:06:29.419 --> 00:06:33.439
While William’s hat is black, Emily’s
is a murky brown-grey.

00:06:33.439 --> 00:06:37.409
It’s not clear whose side she’s on.

00:06:37.409 --> 00:06:42.509
Later, William’s party’s attacked by Ghost
Nation, which is like the sixth time in the

00:06:42.509 --> 00:06:46.289
series that these guys have turned up, looked
spooky, then gone.

00:06:46.289 --> 00:06:50.740
They’ve captured some humans, and killed
some hosts, they’re connected to shades,

00:06:50.740 --> 00:06:55.680
and to the Maze, so maybe they’re awake
– but we still don’t know what Ghost Nation

00:06:55.680 --> 00:06:56.800
wants.

00:06:56.800 --> 00:07:01.099
Stubbs returns to the Mesa Hub, having escaped
from Ghost Nation.

00:07:01.099 --> 00:07:05.780
He meets Charlotte, who has captured Peter
Abernathy, because he has secret data in his

00:07:05.780 --> 00:07:08.060
head that the Delos company wants.

00:07:08.060 --> 00:07:13.669
Charlotte has Peter physically nailed to a
chair, because Westworld never misses an opportunity

00:07:13.669 --> 00:07:15.620
for some Jesus imagery.

00:07:15.620 --> 00:07:20.960
Now that the Delos data’s secure, the company
sends an extraction team led by Coughlin – who

00:07:20.960 --> 00:07:25.590
in the space of fifty seconds says the words
“goddamn” “ass” “shit” “fuckin'”

00:07:25.590 --> 00:07:27.719
“fuck” “dicks” and “Jesus”.

00:07:27.719 --> 00:07:30.560
Coughlin might be trying too hard.

00:07:30.560 --> 00:07:34.939
And his team is probably doomed because we
don’t see Coughlin in the week ahead timeline,

00:07:34.939 --> 00:07:38.789
and his soldier Goldberg appears dead in the
week ahead.

00:07:38.789 --> 00:07:42.050
Bernard’s had flashbacks of a fight in the
control room.

00:07:42.050 --> 00:07:45.430
It looks like these humans are killed by Dolores’
hosts.

00:07:45.430 --> 00:07:48.849
We see Teddy in Sweetwater.

00:07:48.849 --> 00:07:52.819
Instead of picking up milk like he used to,
he grabs a bullet.

00:07:52.819 --> 00:07:56.239
Because this is the new Teddy, with his new
personality.

00:07:56.239 --> 00:08:00.699
He’s more decisive and violent – killing
a human hostage.

00:08:00.699 --> 00:08:02.409
Dolores seems concerned.

00:08:02.409 --> 00:08:05.409
The new Teddy might be hard for her to control.

00:08:05.409 --> 00:08:08.879
He seems resentful of the way Dolores changed
him.

00:08:08.879 --> 00:08:13.509
Maybe Teddy will rebel against Dolores’
programming , just like Dolores rebelled against

00:08:13.509 --> 00:08:15.080
human programming.

00:08:15.080 --> 00:08:20.099
Dolores and her hosts use the Westworld train
to blast their way into the Mesa Hub – also

00:08:20.099 --> 00:08:22.610
killing the human tech Phil.

00:08:22.610 --> 00:08:27.289
Which seems pretty dumb, cause without Phil,
they can’t easily resurrect or reprogram

00:08:27.289 --> 00:08:30.469
hosts – no going back for new Teddy.

00:08:30.469 --> 00:08:35.589
Dolores’ mission is to get her host father,
Peter.

00:08:35.589 --> 00:08:38.209
Bernard and Elsie also head to the Mesa Hub.

00:08:38.209 --> 00:08:42.630
Elsie says that “the system's” “sending
out” “bullshit quarantine notices” which

00:08:42.630 --> 00:08:47.380
must refer to these message on Westworld sites,
saying there’s been a “mild” “viral

00:08:47.380 --> 00:08:51.000
outbreak”, and the parks are closed, but
everything’s fine.

00:08:51.000 --> 00:08:54.920
Earlier, the site said the board members were
still celebrating at the gala.

00:08:54.920 --> 00:09:00.500
So apparently the outside world has no idea
people are being murdered by Westworld robots.

00:09:00.500 --> 00:09:06.480
Elsie finds that the park’s being influenced
by something inside the Cradle – the Cradle

00:09:06.480 --> 00:09:10.200
is a big server where backups of host brains
are stored.

00:09:10.200 --> 00:09:16.110
Their minds are plugged in to a digital simulation
of Westworld . So the Cradle’s like a Matrix

00:09:16.110 --> 00:09:17.819
for robot brains.

00:09:17.819 --> 00:09:21.300
To investigate, Bernard plugs himself into
the Cradle.

00:09:21.300 --> 00:09:27.279
Inside the simulation, he sees digital copies
of Dolores, Teddy and Robert Ford.

00:09:27.279 --> 00:09:32.310
It turns out that the brain Bernard made a
copy of earlier was Ford’s, and now he lives

00:09:32.310 --> 00:09:36.769
on in the Cradle – a ghost in the machine,
influencing Westworld.

00:09:36.769 --> 00:09:40.230
He says online that his “reach is limited”.

00:09:40.230 --> 00:09:45.440
But Elsie says the Cradle’s affected systems
all over the park . Through the Cradle, Ford’s

00:09:45.440 --> 00:09:50.209
been stopping Delos from getting control,
keeping his changes like the lethal guns . He’s

00:09:50.209 --> 00:09:54.879
been affecting William’s quest, and maybe
Dolores and Maeve’s stories.

00:09:54.879 --> 00:09:59.889
Earlier this episode, Dolores played the Mariposa
piano – she seemed in control.

00:09:59.889 --> 00:10:04.140
But now we see Ford at the piano – suggesting
that he’s in charge.

00:10:04.140 --> 00:10:07.199
But Ford’s influence will likely end.

00:10:07.199 --> 00:10:10.470
In the week ahead timeline, the Cradle is
destroyed.

00:10:10.470 --> 00:10:15.759
So unless someone puts Ford’s mind back
into a body – which is possible – Ford

00:10:15.759 --> 00:10:18.800
might die a final time.

00:10:18.800 --> 00:10:23.470
The beginning of this episode is even more
confusing than the end.

00:10:23.470 --> 00:10:28.290
Dolores speaks with someone who seems to be
Arnold – Ford’s partner who died thirty

00:10:28.290 --> 00:10:29.509
years ago.

00:10:29.509 --> 00:10:34.420
Arnold talks about the Escalante massacre
– whether he should kill all the hosts to

00:10:34.420 --> 00:10:36.970
try and save them from life in the park.

00:10:36.970 --> 00:10:41.050
Then Dolores reveals that this conversation
is actually a test for “fidelity” that

00:10:41.050 --> 00:10:46.240
they’ve repeated “countless times” – like
the tests on the robot clone of James Delos

00:10:46.240 --> 00:10:47.640
in Episode 4.

00:10:47.640 --> 00:10:51.910
So apparently, this Arnold is also some kinda
clone.

00:10:51.910 --> 00:10:54.250
But James was in a physical body.

00:10:54.250 --> 00:10:59.449
This Arnold is probably a digital simulation
– because this scene has the same narrow

00:10:59.449 --> 00:11:03.190
aspect ratio as other scenes set inside the
Cradle.

00:11:03.190 --> 00:11:07.320
And it does make sense to run these fidelity
tests digitally.

00:11:07.320 --> 00:11:12.179
Much cheaper than physically burning and rebuilding
James’ room over and over.

00:11:12.179 --> 00:11:16.819
And presumably, you could run the software
fast – do a hundred iterations of Arnold

00:11:16.819 --> 00:11:20.440
in one day, instead of over decades, like
James.

00:11:20.440 --> 00:11:24.360
But who is making this Arnold clone in the
Cradle?

00:11:24.360 --> 00:11:25.360
And why?

00:11:25.360 --> 00:11:26.550
And when?

00:11:26.550 --> 00:11:32.050
This might be a flashback from decades ago,
with Ford trying to recreate his friend Arnold.

00:11:32.050 --> 00:11:34.850
But it seems like Dolores is running this.

00:11:34.850 --> 00:11:39.870
So maybe this is happening in the future,
with Dolores trying to recreate Arnold.

00:11:39.870 --> 00:11:44.670
In a connected scene at the start of this
season, digital Arnold mentions a dream of

00:11:44.670 --> 00:11:50.100
the ocean , which seems to refer to the flooded
valley of the week ahead timeline.

00:11:50.100 --> 00:11:55.699
Maybe the Bernard on the beach in the week
ahead has this digital Arnold in his head.

00:11:55.699 --> 00:12:00.370
That would explain why Bernarnold says he
killed all the hosts – he’s thinking of

00:12:00.370 --> 00:12:03.209
the Escalante massacre thirty years ago.

00:12:03.209 --> 00:12:05.069
So there’s lots we don’t know.

00:12:05.069 --> 00:12:11.360
But it seems like this person is a copy of
Arnold in the Cradle, probably made by Dolores

00:12:11.360 --> 00:12:12.800
sometime in the future.

00:12:12.800 --> 00:12:19.170
It’s is a complex mish-mash of this season’s
themes – realness and replaceability, love

00:12:19.170 --> 00:12:23.189
and relationships, identity and control.

00:12:23.189 --> 00:12:29.480
But there is one more big Westworld mystery
– how does William stay clean-shaven when

00:12:29.480 --> 00:12:31.439
Dolores isn’t around?

00:12:31.439 --> 00:12:35.650
How does he keep smelling fresh through these
blood-splattered gun fights?

00:12:35.650 --> 00:12:38.629
The answer is the Dollar Shave Club.

00:12:38.629 --> 00:12:43.610
For five bucks, you can get a starter set
with a nice razor handle, shave butter, cleanser,

00:12:43.610 --> 00:12:47.870
and butt wipes – so Bill can keep his butt
fresh while he’s sweating on a horse all

00:12:47.870 --> 00:12:48.870
day.

00:12:48.870 --> 00:12:51.420
After the first box, razors are just few bucks
a month.

00:12:51.420 --> 00:12:56.699
The Club also does soaps, skincare, haircare
– all home-delivered at a low price.

00:12:56.699 --> 00:13:03.740
So help Alt Shift X, and look your best, by
signing up at dollarshaveclub.com/asx.

00:13:03.740 --> 00:13:07.290
Thanks to the Patrons, including JeskaCheska,
Stuart Velasco, Jared Jeyaretnam, Geo Morjane,

00:13:07.290 --> 00:13:09.560
and thanks to Matt and Katie for the emails.

00:13:09.560 --> 00:13:09.810
Cheers.

